WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:04.025
This episode focuses on comparisons over time.

2
00:00:04.025 --> 00:00:11.502
Census data becomes useful when the population, measure, geography, and time period are stated before anyone searches for a number.

3
00:00:11.502 --> 00:00:16.939
A change claim needs compatible products, periods, universes, variables, and boundaries.

4
00:00:16.939 --> 00:00:24.414
First confirm that table concepts and question wording remained comparable, then inspect technical notes and annotations.

5
00:00:24.414 --> 00:00:27.453
Test whether the difference exceeds sampling uncertainty.

6
00:00:27.453 --> 00:00:35.076
For dollar measures, decide whether the question concerns nominal or inflation-adjusted change and document the price index and reference year.

7
00:00:35.076 --> 00:00:39.826
Boundary changes can create apparent demographic change without movement by residents.

8
00:00:39.826 --> 00:00:42.422
Use official relationship files where possible.

9
00:00:42.422 --> 00:00:47.614
Avoid overlapping five-year estimates for trend claims when a cleaner comparison is available.

10
00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:49.118
Torrance application segment.

11
00:00:49.118 --> 00:00:52.801
This local application is separate from the Census Academy instruction.

12
00:00:52.801 --> 00:01:04.524
The cited City of Torrance primary source is General Plan, published at https://www.torranceca.gov/Government/Departments-Offices/Departments-Offices/Community-Development/Planning-Division/Comprehensive-Planning/General-Plan.

13
00:01:04.524 --> 00:01:11.215
For a local analysis, date the General Plan baseline, current local records, and ACS periods separately before describing change.

14
00:01:11.215 --> 00:01:18.529
Do not present City policy or administrative records as Census Bureau findings, and do not present a federal estimate as adopted City policy.

15
00:01:18.529 --> 00:01:28.741
Keep a reproducibility packet containing the question, source URLs, exact vintage, table or query, geography codes, raw result, calculations, and uncertainty note.

16
00:01:28.741 --> 00:01:32.061
This narration is an original synthesis of cited U.S.

17
00:01:32.061 --> 00:01:36.947
Census Bureau government works and separately cited City of Torrance material.

18
00:01:36.947 --> 00:01:41.333
Third-party videos, software, graphics, and linked works are excluded.

19
00:01:41.333 --> 00:01:47.472
This product uses Census Bureau information but is not endorsed or certified by the Census Bureau.

20
00:01:47.472 --> 00:01:51.920
It is not an official City product and does not imply City endorsement.
